    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d118">

                <pb facs="0173" n="81" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg81"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Marshal Stalin</hi><anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d118-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">operational priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Aboard the</hi> U. S. S. “<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Iowa</hi>”</placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-12"
                            >12 November 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Personal and secret for Marshal Stalin from the President.</p>
                <p>I am of course made very happy by your telegram of ten November<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d118-f2"/> and the definite prospect of our meeting, and I shall be
                    very glad to see Mr. Molotov in Cairo on the twenty-second. I am just leaving
                    for French North Africa. Warm regards.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d118-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d118-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the United States Naval Attaché, Moscow, via the White House Map Room and
                    Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d118-f2" n="2" xml:id="d118-f2-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg78">p. 78</ref>.</p>
